/**
 * Fills in the "Release Date" column (D) based on a title -> year
 * lookup table. Only fills YEAR, not a specific month/day — exact
 * release dates for 560+ titles (many obscure Korean dramas, anime,
 * and indie films) aren't something that can be reliably recalled to
 * the day from memory, and a wrong specific date is worse than a
 * correct year. Year is the reliable-confidence unit here.
 *
 * *** IMPORTANT CAVEAT ***
 * These years are best-effort from general knowledge, NOT individually
 * verified against a database. Confidence is HIGH for mainstream
 * English-language movies/TV, and LOWER for niche Korean dramas,
 * lesser-known anime, and obscure indie titles — there WILL be some
 * mistakes in that second group. Please spot-check, especially any
 * row with a Korean/Anime title you don't recognize.
 *
 * HOW TO USE:
 * 1. Open your sheet -> Extensions -> Apps Script
 * 2. Add this as a new file (or paste below your existing functions)
 * 3. Run fillReleaseDate()
 * 4. Authorize permissions on first run if prompted
 *
 * Only fills blank Release Date cells — won't overwrite anything
 * you've already entered by hand.
 */

